    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3309A\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the parks, recreation and historic preservation law, in\nrelation to Gold Star families\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow all veterans and members of Gold\nStar families have free access to public campsites, parks, and other\nplaces of recreation in this state.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection amends section 13.19 of the parks, recreation and historic pres-\nervation law to provide veterans and Gold Star families free access to\npublic parks, campsites, and other places of recreation in New York\nState.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAny person who has served in our country's military deserves to be\nhonored and rewarded for their innumerable sacrifices and selfless\nservice. By expanding the Lifetime Liberty Pass to all veterans and Gold\nStar families, we as a state can begin to thank and give back to our\nveterans and their families for all that they have done for us.  Allow-\ning all veterans and members of Gold Star families free access to our\nNew York State Parks will provide them with outdoor spaces to spend time\nwith loved ones and take in the natural beauty of New York State. In\ndoing this, these parks will be highly appreciated and used by people\nwho deserve to be revered for their service to this country. This\nprogram already exists at the federal level with free access to National\nParks, therefore there is no reason that the same program cannot exist\nfor New York State public parks, campsites, and other places of recre-\nation in our beautiful state.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSenate\n\n2021: S5263; Referred to Cultural Affairs, Tourism, Parks and Recreation\n\n2022: S5263; Referred to Cultural Affairs, Tourism, Parks and Recreation\n\nAssembly\n\nNo same as\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of April next succeeding 30 the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
